Description: autotests: Cover stereo pairs that cannot share one commit
 Two outputs paired as a stereo pair share one atomic commit when they are
 on the same GPU. These cases fail today:
 .
 - a pair split over two GPUs presents nothing at all;
 - unpairing, or removing the partner, before it presents leaves the
   first output's frame waiting forever;
 - the pair's commit goes to the commit thread of whichever output
   presented first;
 - the pair's page flip releases a commit the partner's own commit
   thread has in flight.
